[1m[36m▸ 4. Ambient capture — opt-in per source[0m
[2mClipboard, shell history, screenshots, browser history, audio, calendar. Every source is opt-in and revocable. Default first-run: clipboard + shell on, everything else off. State persists to ~/.tracemind/capture_permissions.toml.[0m

[33m$ ./target/release/tracemind capture list[0m
[tracemind] using bundled models from /Users/aadityasrivathsan/Desktop/agent_memory_system/target/release/models (bundle)
on   clipboard   system clipboard (polled; high-entropy strings skipped)
on   shell       shell history (.zsh_history / .bash_history tailing)
on   notes       Apple Notes (macOS, AppleScript dump at backfill)
off  screenshot  screenshots via OS hotkey (OCR + caption, raw image stays local)
off  browser     browser bookmarklet / extension (page url, title, selection)
off  audio       microphone via opt-in hotkey (Whisper-tiny, on-device)
off  calendar    macOS EventKit / Google Calendar (read-only, oauth)
off  pdf         PDFs in a watched folder (~/Downloads; text extracted on-device)
off  email       email from a watched .eml drop folder (subject + body, stays local)
off  photo       photo library EXIF (filename, capture time, GPS; image stays local)

[1m[36m▸ 5. Capture doctor — the honest permission story[0m
[2mReports which sources are actually reachable right now. macOS Safari needs Full Disk Access; the doctor tells you exactly what to grant. On builds with --features macos-screencapture, it also shows whether Vision-framework OCR is compiled in.[0m

[33m$ ./target/release/tracemind capture-doctor 2>&1 | head -25[0m
[tracemind] using bundled models from /Users/aadityasrivathsan/Desktop/agent_memory_system/target/release/models (bundle)
Capture doctor
  [  OK] chrome: history readable
  [PERM] safari: needs Full Disk Access — grant to the daemon binary in System Settings → Privacy & Security → Full Disk Access, then restart `tracemind-capture`
  [  --] screenshot-ocr: unavailable (build with --features macos-screencapture on macOS + Xcode CLI Tools)

To grant Full Disk Access on macOS: open System Settings → Privacy & Security → Full Disk Access, click +, add `tracemind-capture` (and `tracemind` if you also run the CLI probe under launchd), then restart the daemon.

[1m[35m════════════════════════════════════════════════════════[0m
[1m[35m ACT III — Memory backend[0m
[1m[35m════════════════════════════════════════════════════════[0m

[1m[36m▸ 6. Query — bandit-routed retrieval[0m
[2mThe query planner classifies the intent; a contextual bandit (LinUCB with 5 arms — narrow / medium / wide / deep / colbert) picks the retrieval width; results fuse dense (BGE) + BM25 lexical + recency + confidence via ComposedIndex, then ColBERT MaxSim reranks.[0m

[33m$ ./target/release/tracemind query 'world cup tickets'[0m
[tracemind] using bundled models from /Users/aadityasrivathsan/Desktop/agent_memory_system/target/release/models (bundle)
Query: d81c4580-8453-4b12-ad4d-a0e3903ab485
Answer (Extractive, 0ms):
https://www.fifa.com/tickets FIFA World Cup 2026 Tickets

Citations: [1] signal:2, [2] signal:3, [3] signal:4, [4] entity:edf90296-b6b0-4412-adec-659921b97d13, [5] entity:9db742c5-c918-4a01-88eb-517eda2e08e7

  [Product] Tickets
  [Event] FIFA World Cup 2026
  [Url] https://www.fifa.com/tickets
  [Organization] fifa.com
  [Event] World Cup

[1m[36m▸ 7. Ask — tiered answer layer[0m
[2mExtractive Tier 0 always works. Tier 1 (Qwen 2.5 1.5B Q4 GGUF, ~900 MB) and Tier 2 (Apple FoundationModels on macOS 26+) are opt-in features. Answers ground on retrieved entities with citations — abstains rather than hallucinating.[0m

[33m$ ./target/release/tracemind ask 'where can I buy tickets for the 2026 World Cup?'[0m
[tracemind] using bundled models from /Users/aadityasrivathsan/Desktop/agent_memory_system/target/release/models (bundle)
https://www.fifa.com/tickets FIFA World Cup 2026 Tickets

— tier-0 extractive • 0 ms • 5 citation(s)
    [1] signal:2
    [2] signal:3
    [3] signal:7
    [4] signal:1
    [5] signal:8

(hint: Tier-1 weights not present. `tracemind models pull` (~940 MB) unlocks prose answers.)

[1m[36m▸ 8. Quick recall — launcher target (X2/X8)[0m
[2mSub-100ms, small top_k, no LLM. Bind this to a global shortcut in Raycast / Alfred: keystroke → the site you're thinking of, no chrome.[0m

[33m$ ./target/release/tracemind quick-recall 'reflective prompt' --top-k 3[0m
[tracemind] using bundled models from /Users/aadityasrivathsan/Desktop/agent_memory_system/target/release/models (bundle)
   1. [graph] GEPA
   2. [graph] arxiv.org
   3. [graph] TraceMind

[1m[36m▸ 9. Trace — immutable audit trail[0m
[2mEvery ingest + query produces a Trace (UUID, timestamp, content hash, entity IDs) written append-only to traces.jsonl. Ground truth for provenance and rollback.[0m

